    <Label Name="Title" Style="Heading" Text="Chase the Rainbow" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="Explanation" Text="Every rainbow is a circle, and you are standing on the line through its middle. The middle is the shadow of your head: the point straight opposite the sun, which is behind you. The red light comes to you from raindrops 42° away from that point, all the way round. The ground cuts off the bottom of the circle.\n\nDrag the sun in the corner. A low sun gives a tall rainbow; when it climbs past 42° the rainbow sinks out of sight. That is why rainbows come early or late in the day.\n\nNow walk toward the pot of gold. The rainbow walks with you, since it is made by whichever drops are at the right angle from your own eyes. Nobody has ever reached its end.\n\nAbove it, a second bow with its colors reversed, and a darker sky between the two." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
  </Figures>
</Drawing>